| `corpus/projects/bytecode-vm/notes.md` | the measurement table and its sentence | the numbers changed |

## Measured and argued

Measured:

- every instruction count in this report (emulator runs; scripts 01, 03, 05, 06, 08 and the tool);
- the attribution's sums against the emulator (test);
- the spill counts that motivate sharing (script 08 on regex-nfa);
- parity, the reference checks and the test suites (below).

Argued, not measured beyond the checks named:

- that sharing is sound (equal trees of invariant operands have equal values at the preheader); every pipeline
  run in parity and the tests passed its meaning checks with it;
- that the coalescer change is sound (the copy-exception argument); the corpus agrees with r0 under each backend
  option and all together (`IRWB_FULL=1 tests/typed/speed.test.mjs`, below);
- that the union body is right for every reducible multi-latch loop (the definition), beyond the corpus and the
  test program;
- that the estimate fails as a guard because frequencies change with the blocks: the table shows that it fails,
  the reason is my reading of `frequency.ts`.

## Verification

All on the final compiler sources (commit f503708; 6cb091b and later change one test expectation, notes and
this ticket), after `npm run build`:

| Check | Result |
| --- | --- |
| `node tools/parity.mjs` | 50 projects, 135 functions, 8,286 of 8,286 decided cases agree, 14 at the limit, 0 failures (`various/parity-after.log`) |
| `node tools/reference-check.mjs` | reference images: 8,286 of 8,286 agree |
| `node tools/reference-check.mjs --o2` | our O2 images: 8,286 of 8,286 agree |
| `node --test tests/typed/*.test.mjs` | 157 tests, 155 pass, 2 skipped, 0 fail |
| `node --test tests/framework/*.test.mjs` | 234 pass |
| `node --test tests/workbench/*.test.mjs` | 25 tests, 24 pass, 1 skipped, 0 fail |
| `IRWB_FULL=1 node --test tests/typed/speed.test.mjs` | 9 pass: every corpus project agrees with r0 under each backend option and all together |
| `node tools/build-site.mjs` | builds |
| `tools/format-docs.mjs --check`, `tools/format-corpus.mjs --check` | no file would change |

- wrong-shift's `div-to-shift` is rejected in the parity run, as its `broken` pipeline intends.
- One test outside the directories of the brief changed: `tests/workbench/strategies.test.mjs` pinned licm's
  need as `typed.loops@1`; it now expects `@2`. The first workbench run failed on exactly that line.
- Parity was not run at the starting commit; only the instruction baseline (`various/corpus-before.json`) was
  taken there.
- Timing: `attributeSteps` on the VM's `speed` chain (7 revisions) is inside a test that takes about 6 s under a
  machine load above 30, most of it the checked pipeline; the attribution itself was not timed separately.


## Left out

- A value-level attribution (sites are statements; `Program.why` answers for a value).
- A guard in `speed` that picks the pipeline by emulator count: `fastest-all` does that, and it would have hidden
  the loops defect.

## Later

- The coalescer's new exception is per block; copies of one register in different blocks still interfere.
- Projects whose O2 count is above r0 after this work (see the corpus table): candidates for the next stage.
- licm cost: it hoists expressions out of loops that run zero times or that sit on cold paths (chessOrder).
- Attribution over a weighted case set, and to rewrite-rule ids, for the missed-optimization stage.
- constprop raises the count at its own step in 22 functions; whether the pipeline's later passes always take it
  back was not checked per function.
// Measurement: executed RV32 instructions per corpus project at r0 and after O2 and speed, summed over the seeded
// cases `measure` uses (10 per function, seed 7), under the default backend options and under the options `speed`
// is meant for (chains, coalesce, homes). Passes are checked with 5 cases each (parity.mjs does the full check).
// usage: node 03-corpus-measure.mjs out.json [--licm '{"share":true}'] [id...]
import { writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';
import { projectIds, projectFiles } from '../../../../../../tools/corpus.mjs';
import { installVendor } from '../../../../../../tools/node-vendor.mjs';
await installVendor();
const D = '../../../../../../dist/';
const { Program } = await import(D + 'typed/program.js');
const { projectSource } = await import(D + 'typed/project.js');
const { storeOf } = await import(D + 'typed/ir.js');
const { casesFrom } = await import(D + 'typed/evaluate.js');
const { lowerToImage, runImage } = await import(D + 'typed/backend/index.js');

const argv = process.argv.slice(2);
const licmParams = argv.includes('--licm') ? JSON.parse(argv[argv.indexOf('--licm') + 1]) : null;
const [out, ...only] = argv.filter((a, i) => !a.startsWith('--') && argv[i - 1] !== '--licm');
const { PIPELINES } = await import(D + 'typed/passes.js');
const TUNED = { chains: true, coalesce: true, homes: true };
function instructions(p, options) {
  const art = p.head, st = storeOf(art.value);
  const { image } = lowerToImage(art, options);
  let n = 0, limited = 0;
  for (const fn of art.value.fnOrder)
    for (const c of casesFrom(st, fn, { count: 10, seed: 7, inputs: p.inputs[fn] ?? {} })) {
      const r = runImage(image, fn, c.args, c.memory, { limit: 2e5, counts: false });
      if (r.limit || !Number.isFinite(r.steps)) { n += 2e5; limited++; } else n += r.steps;
    }
  return { n, limited };
}
const rows = {};
for (const id of only.length ? only : projectIds()) {
  const ps = projectSource(id, projectFiles(id));
  const row = {};
  try {
    for (const pipeline of ['r0', 'O2', 'speed']) {
      const p = Program.fromProject(ps);
      if (p.status !== 'ok') throw new Error(p.status);
      let rejected = [];
      if (pipeline !== 'r0' && !licmParams) rejected = (await p.pipeline(pipeline, { count: 5 })).steps.filter(s => s.rejected).map(s => s.pass);
      else if (pipeline !== 'r0')
        // the same pipeline pass by pass, with parameters for licm (the experiment switches of scripts/06)
        for (const pass of PIPELINES[pipeline]) {
          try { await p.apply(pass, { count: 5, ...(pass === 'licm' ? { params: licmParams } : {}) }); }
          catch (e) { if (e.code !== 'contractRejected') throw e; rejected.push(pass); }
        }
      const d = instructions(p, {}), t = instructions(p, TUNED);
      row[pipeline] = { default: d.n, tuned: t.n, limited: d.limited, ...(rejected.length ? { rejected } : {}) };
    }
  } catch (e) { row.error = String(e.message).slice(0, 120); }
  rows[id] = row;
  console.log(id.padEnd(24), JSON.stringify(row));
}
writeFileSync(out, JSON.stringify(rows, null, 1) + '\n');
// The report's corpus table from two outputs of 03-corpus-measure.mjs: instructions per project under O2 and
// speed, before and after, default backend options and tuned (chains + coalesce + homes), with totals and every
// cell that got worse. usage: node 09-corpus-table.mjs before.json after.json
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
const [b, a] = process.argv.slice(2).map(f => JSON.parse(readFileSync(f, 'utf8')));
const cols = [['O2', 'default'], ['O2', 'tuned'], ['speed', 'default'], ['speed', 'tuned']];
const n = x => x.toLocaleString('en-US');
const total = { r0d: 0, r0t: 0, b: cols.map(() => 0), a: cols.map(() => 0) };
const worse = [], changed = [], rejected = [];
console.log('| Project | r0 | r0 tuned | O2 | O2 tuned | speed | speed tuned |');
console.log('| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |');
for (const id of Object.keys(b)) {
  const x = b[id], y = a[id];
  if (!y || x.error || y.error) { console.log(`| ${id} | error | | | | | |`); continue; }
  total.r0d += x.r0.default; total.r0t += x.r0.tuned;
  const cells = cols.map(([p, o], i) => {
    total.b[i] += x[p][o]; total.a[i] += y[p][o];
    if (y[p][o] > x[p][o]) worse.push(`${id} ${p}/${o}: ${x[p][o]} -> ${y[p][o]}`);
    return x[p][o] === y[p][o] ? n(x[p][o]) : `${n(x[p][o])} → ${n(y[p][o])}`;
  });
  for (const p of ['O2', 'speed']) if (y[p].rejected) rejected.push(`${id} ${p}: ${y[p].rejected}`);
  if (cells.some(c => c.includes('→'))) changed.push(id);
  console.log(`| ${id} | ${n(x.r0.default)} | ${n(x.r0.tuned)} | ${cells.join(' | ')} |`);
}
console.log(`| **total** | ${n(total.r0d)} | ${n(total.r0t)} | ${cols.map((_, i) => total.b[i] === total.a[i] ? n(total.b[i]) : `${n(total.b[i])} → ${n(total.a[i])}`).join(' | ')} |`);
console.log(`\nchanged: ${changed.join(', ') || 'none'}\nworse: ${worse.join('; ') || 'none'}\nrejected passes: ${rejected.join('; ') || 'none'}`);

